---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Affiliate and commercial disclosure"
  description="Church Software UK's current position on affiliate links, sponsorship, rankings and editorial independence."
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Affiliate disclosure" }]}
>
  <section class="section editorial-page">
    <div class="container prose">
      <header class="article-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">Commercial transparency</p>
        <h1>Affiliate and commercial disclosure</h1>
      </header>
      <div class="notice">
        <p>
          <strong>Current status:</strong> we may use affiliate links where a
          supplier offers a suitable affiliate programme. Each link is clearly
          labelled where it appears. Sponsored listings may also be accepted,
          but none is currently published.
        </p>
      </div>
      <h2>How affiliate links are handled</h2>
      <p>
        Where a supplier offers an affiliate programme and we use it, the link
        is labelled at the point of use and the relevant product listing records
        the relationship. We may earn a commission if a qualifying purchase is
        made through one of those links.
      </p>
      <p>
        An affiliate relationship or commission does not affect whether a
        product is included, its position in the directory, shortlist or
        comparison results, its ranking, or its editorial review. It cannot buy
        a positive assessment, remove legitimate caveats or change the evidence
        we use.
      </p>
      <p>
        Any sponsored listing will be labelled clearly on its own product page.
        Sponsorship does not alter the research standard, source requirements,
        ranking or editorial review.
      </p>
      <h2>Inclusion is not endorsement</h2>
      <p>
        A listing means the product is relevant enough to research. It does not
        mean the directory recommends it for every church.
      </p>
      <h2>No unsupported rankings</h2>
      <p>
        The site does not publish an overall score or “best” badge. A meaningful
        ranking would need visible criteria, supporting evidence and a method
        that respects different church contexts.
      </p>
      <h2>How to raise a concern</h2>
      <p>
        If a factual statement, label or commercial disclosure appears wrong,
        please use the supplier update route and include public evidence. We
        assess corrections against the evidence provided; commercial status does
        not determine the outcome. Read the <a href="/methodology/">research methodology</a>
        for the distinction between supplier information and directory assessment.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
